SCHEDULE: {"1":"Gus","2":"Cara","3":"Ann","4":"Ben","5":"Finn","6":"Elif","7":"Dev"}
CONFIDENCE: 97

The constraints chain together as Gus < Cara < Finn < Elif < Dev. Finn can't be in slot 3, so Finn is in 4 or 5, and Dev can't be in 6, so Dev is in 7. That leaves Finn in 5 with Elif in 6, or Finn in 4 with Elif in 5. The second case has no valid placement for Ann, Ben, Gus and Cara. In the first case, Ann and Ben must take slots 3 and 4, since Ben can't be in 3 and Ann can't be in 4. That forces Gus into 1 and Cara into 2. I checked every constraint against this schedule and the solution is unique.
